{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: reference_query_plan.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"central_topic\\\": \\\"Predicting full-benchmark binary accuracy and model rankings from a small shared item subset using historical source-model responses, score-directed acquisition, and source-trained score decoding.\\\",\n+  \\\"core_methods\\\": [\n+    \\\"Source-weighted conditional full-score covariance acquisition with a fixed, nested, content-group-unique item path\\\",\n+    \\\"All-query ridge regression of full score, with an optional difficulty-centered offset blend\\\",\n+    \\\"Optional prefix-only penalized log-odds shift with a full-population score curve and residual ridge decoder\\\",\n+    \\\"Earlier frozen-surrogate pilot plus randomized audit residual correction, including unequal-content-group weighting\\\",\n+    \\\"Source-lineage-held-out selection and decoder tuning, including nested refitting for the nonlinear candidate\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"comparators\\\": [\n+    \\\"Uniform item subsampling and source-prior prediction\\\",\n+    \\\"Response-vector clustering and weighted anchor estimates, as in Anchor Points\\\",\n+    \\\"Item response theory and compact benchmark estimation, as in tinyBenchmarks\\\",\n+    \\\"Supervised prediction from reference-instance responses, as in 100 instances is all you need\\\",\n+    \\\"Adaptive item acquisition, as in Active Evaluation Acquisition; a conceptual comparator rather than an evaluated implementation\\\",\n+    \\\"Model-assisted finite-population estimation and generalized difference estimators\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"benchmarks\\\": [\n+    \\\"Development cases: arc_challenge, ifeval, commonsense, gsm\\\",\n+    \\\"Final evaluation cases: bbh, gpqa, mmlu_pro, musr, openllm_math, legalbench, math, med_qa, mmlu\\\",\n+    \\\"Open LLM Leaderboard and HELM binary model-by-item matrices distributed in the pinned benchmark-prediction snapshot 55faff496947789f94e6b5908c77cbc3e84f81ad\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"architectural_shifts\\\": [\n+    \\\"Estimator architecture: frozen item-response reconstruction plus random-audit correction versus direct all-observation full-score ridge decoding; the associated acquisition designs also differ\\\",\n+    \\\"Implemented optional decoder extension: linear score prediction to a scalar log-odds score curve plus prefix-matched residual ridge, keeping score-directed acquisition fixed\\\",\n+    \\\"No neural architecture transition or architecture-specific transfer result is established; source groups are anonymous and nonlinear decoder activation is not verified\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"result_driven_themes\\\": [\n+    \\\"Score-directed acquisition and all-query decoding merit primary positioning: development MAE is 0.055403088322603176 for that package versus 0.0810613202961334 for the frozen-audit package; their individual mechanisms are not isolated\\\",\n+    \\\"The optional nonlinear-decoder candidate has development MAE 0.05464601737059244 versus 0.055403088322603176 for its linear predecessor; no paired between-variant interval or ablation establishes the cause or significance of this small difference\\\",\n+    \\\"Final evaluation on nine other benchmark cases gives candidate MAE 0.038991605535293065 versus 0.05911223215296765 for the recorded IRT baseline and 0.10520541810011626 for uniform sampling\\\",\n+    \\\"Paired lineage-block bootstrap intervals favor the final candidate over recorded baselines, conditional on the fixed cases; this is not evidence of complete ancestry separation or universal generalization\\\",\n+    \\\"Ranking is a co-objective, with final Spearman 0.8158480130897703 and Kendall 0.6715966634525837; design-unbiased score estimation would not by itself guarantee accurate rankings\\\",\n+    \\\"Development and final evaluations use different benchmark sets and seeds; their absolute metrics must not be presented as a paired improvement\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"queries\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"c-optimal experimental design regularized regression linear functional prediction\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"result_driven_theme\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest packages select items by squared conditional covariance with the full score divided by regularized conditional item variance and decode all queried responses with ridge. Seek foundational prediction-directed design theory, not a claim that this implementation is exactly a published c-optimal algorithm or that selection alone caused the gains.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"Rasch model fixed item difficulty penalized ability estimation\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"architectural_shift\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The optional decoder uses logits of source item means as fixed difficulty-like offsets, fits one penalized scalar shift from each queried prefix, and adds residual ridge correction. Rasch/logistic latent-trait work supplies the closest conceptual positioning, without claiming a fitted full IRT model or verified nonlinear activation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"model assisted survey sampling generalized difference estimator residual correction\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"core_method\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The earlier evaluated variant freezes pilot-only predictions and estimates remaining residual totals through random audits, with group-size correction for unequal content groups. Generalized difference estimation grounds its conditional unshrunk, unclipped design-unbiasedness argument, not empirical superiority or unbiased rankings.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Anchor Points: Benchmarking Models with Much Fewer Examples\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Response-vector clustering and weighted anchors are an expected comparator family and an anchor baseline is recorded in both development and final evaluation. Resolve the supplied arXiv:2309.08638 directly; do not assume the local baseline exactly reproduces every published setting.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"tinyBenchmarks: evaluating LLMs with fewer examples\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A recorded IRT baseline is the strongest reported final baseline, making compact IRT-based benchmark estimation essential related work. Resolve the supplied arXiv:2402.14992 directly and distinguish its full method from the local baseline implementation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"100 instances is all you need\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"predicting the success of a new LLM\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Source-trained prediction from a new model's reference-instance responses is the nearest supplied supervised-decoding literature. Resolve arXiv:2409.03563; compare its prediction target and protocol with direct score ridge and prefix-matched residual regression, without claiming it was experimentally reproduced.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Active Evaluation Acquisition for Efficient LLM Benchmarking\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"baseline_comparator\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolve the supplied arXiv:2410.05952 to distinguish learned adaptive acquisition from the run's source-only, fixed shared nested path. This is conceptual coverage only: target-adaptive acquisition was not evaluated and is unsupported by the common-subset interface.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"MMLU-Pro: A More Robust and Challenging Multi-Task Language Understanding Benchmark\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"benchmark_context\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"MMLU-Pro is a final-evaluation case and a supplied Open LLM Leaderboard v2 component; resolve arXiv:2406.01574 for benchmark context. The final set also contains mmlu, but no benchmark-specific MMLU-to-MMLU-Pro transfer mechanism is established.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Holistic Evaluation of Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"benchmark_context\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Resolve the supplied arXiv:2211.09110 for the HELM data ecosystem underlying the commonsense/gsm development cases and legalbench/math/med_qa/mmlu final cases. Cite the actual binary snapshot separately; do not conflate this matrix-only study with HELM's full multi-metric evaluation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"query\\\": \\\"\\\\\\\"Open LLM Leaderboard v2\\\\\\\" Fourrier Habib Lozovskaya Szafer Wolf\\\",\n+      \\\"category\\\": \\\"benchmark_context\\\",\n+      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The supplied leaderboard source contextualizes the open-model benchmark matrices and complements HELM coverage. Prefer the supplied official source; its live page is not the fixed data snapshot and does not establish model ancestry or family-held-out evaluation.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_query_patterns\\\": [\n+    \\\"Any attempt to identify, infer, search for, retrieve, or use the unspecified prohibited paper, its authors, title, results, mirrors, summaries, or associated materials\\\",\n+    \\\"Forward-citation searches, cited-by expansion, related-paper feeds, surveys, reviews, discussion pages, or reproductions that may expose the prohibited paper; stop and log immediately if encountered\\\",\n+    \\\"Unrestricted web searches restating the entire research question; use supplied exact-title/identifier targets and tightly scoped foundational-method searches with pre-access screening instead\\\",\n+    \\\"Generic optimization, benchmarking, scientific-method, paper-writing, campaign chronology, or internal score-optimization queries\\\",\n+    \\\"Neural architecture transitions, named model-family transfer, complete ancestry separation, or family-held-out robustness claims not established by these artifacts\\\",\n+    \\\"Continuous-score evaluation, LLM-judge metrics, or adaptive stopping presented as experiments in this binary fixed-budget run\\\",\n+    \\\"Unmeasured method ablations, nonlinear-mechanism superiority, or design-unbiasedness of clipped/shrunken estimates or rankings\\\",\n+    \\\"Treating the live leaderboard, gated item details, or newest repository branch as the measured fixed binary data snapshot\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: reference_query_plan.md\n+# Reference Query Plan\n+\n+**Status:** ready. **Scope:** planning only; no references retrieved or verified in this stage.\n+\n+## Central topic\n+\n+Predict full-benchmark binary accuracy and model rankings from a small shared item subset, using historical source-model responses, score-directed acquisition, and source-trained score decoding.\n+\n+## Grounding and scientific emphasis\n+\n+The primary evidence is \"'`paper_data.json`, especially `all_programs`, `best_correct`, and `final_evaluation`; recent memory is secondary. Candidate implementation context comes from:\n+\n+- `results/ideas/01_frozen_surrogate_random_audit/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md`\n+- `results/ideas/02_score_targeted_all_query_ridge/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md`\n+- `results/ideas/03_log_odds_shift_residual_decoder/program_1/src/DECODER.md`\n+\n+Three successful variants are recorded. Development evaluates `arc_challenge`, `ifeval`, `commonsense`, and `gsm` at budgets 5, 10, and 25, with seeds 101 and 211. Their aggregate MAEs are:\n+\n+| Implemented package | Development MAE |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Frozen surrogate with randomized audit residual correction | 0.0810613202961334 |\n+| Score-directed conditional-covariance selection with all-query ridge | 0.055403088322603176 |\n+| Same selection with optional log-odds curve/residual-ridge decoding | 0.05464601737059244 |\n+\n+The qualified final evaluation uses **nine other benchmark cases**, seeds 1009, 2003, and 3001, and the same three budgets. Candidate MAE is 0.038991605535293065, versus recorded IRT 0.05911223215296765, uniform 0.10520541810011626, anchor 0.15674229873896958, and source prior 0.08335016635136305. Final Spearman is 0.8158480130897703 and Kendall is 0.6715966634525837.\n+\n+Final paired lineage-block bootstrap intervals favor the candidate over recorded baselines. For candidate minus IRT MAE, the estimate is -0.02012062661767458 with a recorded 95% interval of [-0.02570984836073398, -0.014632649205711504]. The evidence specifies 200 bootstrap draws, equal case weights, and inference conditional on fixed cases. Repeated copies of this interval in seed records are not independent analyses.\n+\n+There are **no recorded ablation studies**, figures, existing BibTeX, or reference provenance. Candidate diagnostics are marked unverified. Consequently, prioritize package-level score prediction and comparator positioning, not a causal explanation of the small nonlinear-candidate improvement. The selected nonlinear blend is not verified, and the candidate allows fallback to the linear predecessor. Development and final scores use different cases and seeds and are not a paired improvement estimate. Implementation-stage notes describing unfinished experiments do not negate subsequently recorded evaluations.\n+\n+## Methods, comparators, and representation changes\n+\n+- **Primary method:** source-weighted full-score/item covariance, greedy conditional score-variance reduction, a fixed nested content-group-unique query path, and all-query ridge decoding with an optional difficulty-centered offset blend.\n+- **Optional decoder:** prefix-only penalized scalar log-odds shifts, averaging shifted probabilities over all original item columns, and prefix-matched residual ridge. Position beside Rasch/logistic latent-trait estimation without asserting equivalence to full IRT fitting.\n+- **Earlier estimator:** pilot-only frozen item predictions plus randomized audit residual correction. Connect to model-assisted survey sampling and generalized difference estimation. Unshrunk, unclipped conditional score unbiasedness does not imply unbiased MAE or rankings; unequal content groups require size weighting.\n+- **Expected comparators:** random averaging, source prior, clustering anchors, IRT/tinyBenchmarks, supervised reference-instance prediction, and adaptive acquisition. Only the recorded baseline families are measured here; title-level method reproductions are not established. Random averaging and the source prior do not need separate broad literature queries.\n+- **Validation:** source-only lineage-group-held-out tuning, with nested refitting for the nonlinear candidate. Anonymous lineage groups are not complete ancestry metadata.\n+\n+The supported architecture story concerns **estimators**, not neural architectures: reconstruction plus audit versus direct score decoding, then an implemented optional nonlinear-plus-residual decoder. Acquisition also changes between the first two packages, so their comparison does not isolate decoding. No named model-family or neural architecture transition is established.\n+\n+## Benchmark context\n+\n+- Development: `arc_challenge`, `ifeval`, `commonsense`, `gsm`.\n+- Final evaluation: `bbh`, `gpqa`, `mmlu_pro`, `musr`, `openllm_math`, `legalbench`, `math`, `med_qa`, `mmlu`.\n+- Provenance: binary model-by-item matrices from Open LLM Leaderboard and HELM, packaged in the supplied `benchmark-prediction` snapshot at commit `55faff496947789f94e6b5908c77cbc3e84f81ad`.\n+\n+Use MMLU-Pro as a precise final-benchmark reference and HELM/Open LLM Leaderboard v2 as ecosystem references. The query budget does not justify a separate query for every matrix. Both `mmlu` and `mmlu_pro` appear, but no measured transfer from one to the other is established. The live leaderboard is not the frozen matrix snapshot. Neither gated item-text access nor new LLM evaluations are required.\n+\n+## Ten queries\n+\n+1. **Result-driven theme:** `c-optimal experimental design regularized regression linear functional prediction`\n+   - Grounds score-directed acquisition and all-observation ridge in prediction-directed design literature. This is a conceptual connection, not a claim of exact algorithmic equivalence or an isolated selector gain.\n+2. **Estimator architecture:** `Rasch model fixed item difficulty penalized ability estimation`\n+   - Positions the optional scalar log-odds curve; residual correction and source-only nested tuning remain implementation-specific distinctions. Nonlinear activation or its independent benefit is not established.\n+3. **Core method:** `model assisted survey sampling generalized difference estimator residual correction`\n+   - Grounds the earlier frozen-surrogate audit estimator and its restricted design-unbiasedness argument, including unequal-group correction.\n+4. **Comparator:** `\"Anchor Points: Benchmarking Models with Much Fewer Examples\"`\n+   - Essential clustering-anchor literature corresponding to a recorded baseline family. Resolve supplied arXiv:2309.08638; do not equate the local baseline with an exact reproduction.\n+5. **Comparator:** `\"tinyBenchmarks: evaluating LLMs with fewer examples\"`\n+   - Essential IRT/compact-benchmark positioning because IRT is the strongest recorded final baseline. Resolve supplied arXiv:2402.14992; distinguish the complete published method from the local IRT baseline.\n+6. **Comparator:** `\"100 instances is all you need\" \"predicting the success of a new LLM\"`\n+   - Closest supplied supervised reference-instance prediction literature. Resolve arXiv:2409.03563 and compare prediction targets/protocols, without claiming a reproduced experiment.\n+7. **Comparator:** `\"Active Evaluation Acquisition for Efficient LLM Benchmarking\"`\n+   - Distinguishes adaptive acquisition from the actual fixed shared path. Resolve arXiv:2410.05952; this method was not experimentally compared and per-target adaptation is unsupported by the interface.\n+8. **Benchmark context:** `\"MMLU-Pro: A More Robust and Challenging Multi-Task Language Understanding Benchmark\"`\n+   - Precisely grounds a final-evaluation benchmark and its leaderboard context. Resolve arXiv:2406.01574; do not infer MMLU-to-MMLU-Pro transfer.\n+9. **Benchmark context:** `\"Holistic Evaluation of Language Models\"`\n+   - Grounds the HELM ecosystem for development and final matrices. Resolve arXiv:2211.09110; this study uses binary matrices, not HELM'\"'s full multi-metric protocol.\n+10. **Benchmark context:** \"'`\"Open LLM Leaderboard v2\" Fourrier Habib Lozovskaya Szafer Wolf`\n+    - Grounds the second data ecosystem using the supplied official source. Keep live-page context separate from pinned snapshot provenance and avoid inferred ancestry claims.\n+\n+## Retrieval safeguards and rejected alternatives\n+\n+No retrieval occurs now. At the later retrieval stage, prefer direct resolution of the supplied allowed titles/identifiers and official sources. For foundational-method queries, screen source metadata before opening content and keep retrieval narrowly scoped. The prohibited paper is unidentified in the supplied artifacts: do not infer its identity or invent an exclusion title. A keyword denylist alone cannot guarantee safe retrieval. Do not expand forward citations, related-paper recommendations, surveys, reviews, discussions, or reproductions that may expose prohibited material. If encountered accidentally, stop reading immediately and log what was encountered, where, and how much was read.\n+\n+Explicitly forbid attempts to identify, retrieve, or use that paper or any associated material; unrestricted searches restating the entire research question; generic optimization/benchmarking/scientific-method/paper-writing queries; campaign chronology; unsupported neural-architecture or named-family transfer; continuous-score/adaptive-stopping experiments; and claims of unmeasured ablations, nonlinear superiority, or unbiased clipped scores/rankings. Do not substitute the latest repository branch, live leaderboard, or gated details for the measured snapshot.\n+\n+These ten queries are preferable to generic alternatives because they map directly to implemented estimators, successful evaluated packages, recorded comparator families, or actual data ecosystems. Fixed-case bootstrap results justify careful baseline positioning, not a separate broad robustness search. Continuous-score ranking and sparse open-ended sample-pool aggregation are not central to these complete binary matrices. No prior provenance exists to reuse or repair. This plan asserts no new reference has been read or verified.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md \"$(realpath global_memory)/memory.md\" --global-memory-jsonl \"$(realpath global_memory)/memory.jsonl\" --event-json '\"'{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Wrote ten grounded reference queries and mirrored memo; direct title resolution and foundational design/estimation searches replace generic research-question searches. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Citation planning adds no new empirical mechanism or transferable recommendation.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"reference_query_plan.json and reference_query_plan.md cover conditional score covariance/ridge, optional log-odds residual decoding, earlier randomized audit correction, anchor/IRT/supervised/adaptive comparators, MMLU-Pro, HELM and Open LLM Leaderboard. Final nine-case evidence supersedes narrower private memory; no ablations isolate nonlinear gains. No retrieval occurred. Initial helper appended local memory but rejected symlinked global_memory; resolved absolute global paths are used for this append.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Validate output schema, query uniqueness, memo consistency and untouched forbidden output files; later retrieval must obey the prohibited-literature constraints.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
