ard is not the frozen matrix snapshot. Neither gated item-text access nor new LLM evaluations are required.\n+\n+## Ten queries\n+\n+1. **Result-driven theme:** `c-optimal experimental design regularized regression linear functional prediction`\n+   - Grounds score-directed acquisition and all-observation ridge in prediction-directed design literature. This is a conceptual connection, not a claim of exact algorithmic equivalence or an isolated selector gain.\n+2. **Estimator architecture:** `Rasch model fixed item difficulty penalized ability estimation`\n+   - Positions the optional scalar log-odds curve; residual correction and source-only nested tuning remain implementation-specific distinctions. Nonlinear activation or its independent benefit is not established.\n+3. **Core method:** `model assisted survey sampling generalized difference estimator residual correction`\n+   - Grounds the earlier frozen-surrogate audit estimator and its restricted design-unbiasedness argument, including unequal-group correction.\n+4. **Comparator:** `\"Anchor Points: Benchmarking Models with Much Fewer Examples\"`\n+   - Essential clustering-anchor literature corresponding to a recorded baseline family. Resolve supplied arXiv:2309.08638; do not equate the local baseline with an exact reproduction.\n+5. **Comparator:** `\"tinyBenchmarks: evaluating LLMs with fewer examples\"`\n+   - Essential IRT/compact-benchmark positioning because IRT is the strongest recorded final baseline. Resolve supplied arXiv:2402.14992; distinguish the complete published method from the local IRT baseline.\n+6. **Comparator:** `\"100 instances is all you need\" \"predicting the success of a new LLM\"`\n+   - Closest supplied supervised reference-instance prediction literature. Resolve arXiv:2409.03563 and compare prediction targets/protocols, without claiming a reproduced experiment.\n+7. **Comparator:** `\"Active Evaluation Acquisition for Efficient LLM Benchmarking\"`\n+   - Distinguishes adaptive acquisition from the actual fixed shared path. Resolve arXiv:2410.05952; this method was not experimentally compared and per-target adaptation is unsupported by the interface.\n+8. **Benchmark context:** `\"MMLU-Pro: A More Robust and Challenging Multi-Task Language Understanding Benchmark\"`\n+   - Precisely grounds a final-evaluation benchmark and its leaderboard context. Resolve arXiv:2406.01574; do not infer MMLU-to-MMLU-Pro transfer.\n+9. **Benchmark context:** `\"Holistic Evaluation of Language Models\"`\n+   - Grounds the HELM ecosystem for development and final matrices. Resolve arXiv:2211.09110; this study uses binary matrices, not HELM'\"'s full multi-metric protocol.\n+10. **Benchmark context:** \"'`\"Open LLM Leaderboard v2\" Fourrier Habib Lozovskaya Szafer Wolf`\n+    - Grounds the second data ecosystem using the supplied official source. Keep live-page context separate from pinned snapshot provenance and avoid inferred ancestry claims.\n+\n+## Retrieval safeguards and rejected alternatives\n+\n+No retrieval occurs now. At the later retrieval stage, prefer direct resolution of the supplied allowed titles/identifiers and official sources. For foundational-method queries, screen source metadata before opening content and keep retrieval narrowly scoped. The prohibited paper is unidentified in the supplied artifacts: do not infer its identity or invent an exclusion title. A keyword denylist alone cannot guarantee safe retrieval. Do not expand forward citations, related-paper recommendations, surveys, reviews, discussions, or reproductions that may expose prohibited material. If encountered accidentally, stop reading immediately and log what was encountered, where, and how much was read.\n+\n+Explicitly forbid attempts to identify, retrieve, or use that paper or any associated material; unrestricted searches restating the entire research question; generic optimization/benchmarking/scientific-method/paper-writing queries; campaign chronology; unsupported neural-architecture or named-family transfer; continuous-score/adaptive-stopping experiments; and claims of unmeasured ablations, nonlinear superiority, or unbiased clipped scores/rankings. Do not substitute the latest repository branch, live leaderboard, or gated details for the measured snapshot.\n+\n+These ten queries are preferable to generic alternatives because they map directly to implemented estimators, successful evaluated packages, recorded comparator families, or actual data ecosystems. Fixed-case bootstrap results justify careful baseline positioning, not a separate broad robustness search. Continuous-score ranking and sparse open-ended sample-pool aggregation are not central to these complete binary matrices. No prior provenance exists to reuse or repair. This plan asserts no new reference has been read or verified.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\npython .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md \"$(realpath global_memory)/memory.md\" --global-memory-jsonl \"$(realpath global_memory)/memory.jsonl\" --event-json '\"'{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Wrote ten grounded reference queries and mirrored memo; direct title resolution and foundational design/estimation searches replace generic research-question searches. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Citation planning adds no new empirical mechanism or transferable recommendation.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"reference_query_plan.json and reference_query_plan.md cover conditional score covariance/ridge, optional log-odds residual decoding, earlier randomized audit correction, anchor/IRT/supervised/adaptive comparators, MMLU-Pro, HELM and Open LLM Leaderboard. Final nine-case evidence supersedes narrower private memory; no ablations isolate nonlinear gains. No retrieval occurred. Initial helper appended local memory but rejected symlinked global_memory; resolved absolute global paths are used for this append.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Validate output schema, query uniqueness, memo consistency and untouched forbidden output files; later retrieval must obey the prohibited-literature constraints.\\\"}'\"","aggregated_output":"/bin/sh: 1: apply_patch: not found\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
